Hi,

I'm using a small test sample with only 10k paired-end reads in them. However, the reference sequences and the annotation files are 7.5 GB and 571MB, respectively. The data are not yet published so I'd rather not share them via link here in the discussion grop. Contact me if you want to access them. I can share some basic information about the reference sequences in the meantime, maybe this can provide some insight as to why it is so slow:

Each reference sequence is annotated with a single gene_id, across its entire length.
The sequence lengths are varying between 109-45500 bases, with a mean of 485 and a median of 643.
The sequence header lengths vary between 30-57 characters in length, with a mean of 45 and a median of 43.
Thanks for your time looking into this.

Best,
Fredrik

